3$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379777} {:answer/id #uuid "80b9acca-9fa4-58b6-aa49-2d9e3782664e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Trains** | **Cars** |\n| To: | **Trains** | $0.67$ | $0.58$ |\n| **Cars** | $0.33$ | $0.42$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Trains** | **Cars** |\n| To: | **Trains** | $0.58$ | $0.33$ |\n| **Cars** | $0.42$ | $0.67$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379776} :answer-field/id #uuid "58a1eda3-e0ea-5cdd-878b-61ab3abea02a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379773}] :question/id #uuid "78ea34aa-4300-5834-9be1-24f93a7226aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-35787" :question/problem "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who use trains to travel and those who use cars. A study has shown that, each year \n\n- $42%$ of people who used trains swap to cars, and\n\n- $33%$ of people who used cars swap to trains.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these people change their preferences each year?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year: \n\n- $42%$ of people who used trains swap to cars. This implies that $58%$ of them remain using trains.\n\n- $33%$ of people who used cars swap to trains. This implies that $67%$ of them remain using cars.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Trains** | **Cars** |\n| To: | **Trains** | $0.58$ | $0.33$ |\n| **Cars** | $0.42$ | $0.67$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.58 & 0.33 \\\\ 0.42 & 0.67\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daa07dd-689b-5d68-a711-77459bc9f7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122079} {:answer/id #uuid "c40ed3ab-fd7f-589e-9bca-e8611878bb22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122080} {:answer/id #uuid "22e0d828-15f0-56a1-944a-243f28fd0241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122081} {:answer/id #uuid "44d59735-fe69-523e-810e-154c352fc2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122082} {:answer/id #uuid "45ca4e96-0cfd-54e5-a7fc-d0e7ec0255f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122082} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3b787ef-0c6d-5613-ae18-c431681bcaa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122078}] :question/id #uuid "f54c1f29-b43d-5f0e-a558-1fd0e7509f92" :question/math-academy-id "q-35791" :question/problem "There are three groups of fans in a certain town: those who prefer basketball, those who prefer baseball, and those who prefer football. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the people that prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football,\n\n- from the people that prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball,\n\n- from the people that prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & a \\\\ 0.32 & b & 0.65 \\\\ c & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the people who prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer basketball.\n\n- From people who prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer baseball.\n\n- From people who prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball. This implies that $10%$ of them continue to prefer football.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.32$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.32 & 0.4 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.28 & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.4+0.28=0.93.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b27109-6915-5c9f-b0ea-9aee35a64275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.42$ | $0.65$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.58$ | $0.35$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267286} {:answer/id #uuid "8e695b59-88b3-51a1-92ad-f0a3cb616973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267412} {:answer/id #uuid "e13d09a8-0a4e-5a60-a304-cf6f4763901b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.58$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.42$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268131} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4a1176-e6b7-5d81-bafd-99a441fed0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.35$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.65$ | $0.58$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268271} {:answer/id #uuid "fd69bc48-90ce-5dad-b92a-3165b7d08314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.42$ | $0.35$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.58$ | $0.65$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267412} :answer-field/id #uuid "7451022a-e635-5fae-aac4-1f90cd9a365e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268625}] :question/id #uuid "9a74ecb8-81c8-5154-b418-5e469935a079" :question/math-academy-id "q-135554" :question/problem "There are two groups of children in a certain city: those who prefer ice cream and those who prefer cakes. A study has shown that, each week\n\n- from the children that prefer ice cream, $35%$ change to cakes, and\n\n- from the children that prefer cakes, $42%$ change to ice cream.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these children change their preferences each week?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each week: \n\n- $35%$ of children who preferred ice creams swap to cakes. This implies that $65%$ of them continue to prefer ice creams.\n\n- $42%$ of children who preferred cakes swap to ice creams. This implies that $58%$ of them continue to prefer cakes.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.65 & 0.42 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.58\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2963d02f-b363-5a0f-aa27-a80d676a2f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266508} {:answer/id #uuid "31423e93-11a3-51d2-8443-b149c1469993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266578} {:answer/id #uuid "44263db8-02b1-51d2-8ce3-099afaf36a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266752} {:answer/id #uuid "88e2c516-c2e0-50b6-a880-b9147f8c4f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267361} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8db873-8f0e-54bc-9410-a5b08df1e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267361} :answer-field/id #uuid "7145001a-ff44-5f27-88df-e95dba683bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268617}] :question/id #uuid "16f6ef41-f784-5aac-bb4c-b2858ff4b290" :question/math-academy-id "q-135565" :question/problem "A study shows that for a particular area in a specific season,\n\n- on a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & b & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & c\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for this area:\n\n- On a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $40%$ chance of not having precipitation on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $55%$ chance of having rain on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain. This implies a $45%$ chance of having snow on this day.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **No Precipitation** | **Rain** | **Snow** |\n| To: | **No Precipitation** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| **Rain** | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.05$ |  |\n| **Snow** | $0.35$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.4 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & 0.55 & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & 0.45\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.4+0.55+0.45=1.4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269084 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c287be-ea57-55ce-baae-51bb45b38516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266167} {:answer/id #uuid "08deed52-4468-549e-81a6-f5ab7a3737e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266226} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac975b8-b27b-535d-a06f-1ef6ec9db9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266369} {:answer/id #uuid "50883166-e1a2-56c0-81b4-b76e3dee6317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} {:answer/id #uuid "db8543f6-e928-54f8-a113-98e22acbcee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed26647f-f52c-560b-b302-af5032a00378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268819}] :question/id #uuid "40ee85ea-08ea-5955-8652-e4607e79ae86" :question/math-academy-id "q-135566" :question/problem "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3ecc879-2c95-5f74-ac4a-ab969113e91a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378680} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a103d0-014c-5342-a350-b00b3703cd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378681} {:answer/id #uuid "778b5f63-aa15-579f-aa01-22ef9920862f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- 