of them remain using oil $B.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Oil $A$** | **Oil $B$** |\n| To: | **Oil $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Oil $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88e5b5b4-2dbb-5da4-824a-44c309ccb154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400732} {:answer/id #uuid "574fb5f8-e987-5592-8f6a-6ba872092af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400733} {:answer/id #uuid "b19ea57e-8f9d-5793-af8d-9ddd67581e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.38$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.62$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400734} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb01000-d1a6-589d-b667-eb5990cf355b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400735} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ff6028-9b02-5c55-82e5-4d5c90199599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.62$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.38$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400732} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c6e082-8a7d-505f-8ba1-4c75352ff93e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400731}] :question/id #uuid "27fa3263-36e3-5305-83f8-d0188906560c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135556" :question/problem "A study shows that in a particular region\n\n- there is a $62%$ chance of another rainy day after a rainy day, and\n\n- there is a $55%$ chance of another dry day after a dry day.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how the weather changes?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each day: \n\n- If it is rainy today, there is a $62%$ chance it will be rainy tomorrow. This implies that if it is rainy today, there is a $38%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow.\n\n- If it is dry today, there is a $55%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow. This implies that if it is dry today, there is a $45%$ chance that it will be rainy tomorrow\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15baaae5-2034-5f50-a24b-ecbfa20a7606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402470} {:answer/id #uuid "3ede10a9-b4b5-5ce6-b1dd-ee8a5febfa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402471} {:answer/id #uuid "62a55541-88ec-5f20-a871-b5d459daef1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.45$ | $0.62$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.55$ | $0.38$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402472} {:answer/id #uuid "90bc75c0-d406-5d4b-a7dc-ab4038a5be06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402473} {:answer/id #uuid "06612a8f-9269-5aad-b8a3-a061a85388f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.45$ | $0.38$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.55$ | $0.62$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402471} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb43538b-a251-5a95-8548-eb479e6f2a90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402469}] :question/id #uuid "96e846e9-ab89-5268-ba2a-aaad5210df91" :question/math-academy-id "q-35843" :question/problem "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who are healthy and those who are sick. A study has shown that each quarter\n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick, and\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how people's health status changes?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each semester: \n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick. This implies that $62%$ of them remain healthy.\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health. This implies that $55%$ of them remain sick.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d1b8c-2c04-568e-8da7-51e6ea7c8663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Countryside</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.72$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.88$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550444} {:answer/id #uuid "6971dc04-f2d9-5e4d-af65-09fc1da42a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"