number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e96d429-426d-57be-9829-ac4f3df0f0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465657} {:answer/id #uuid "63d8e8dc-2cdc-5569-842a-a09fd62da3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465657} :answer-field/id #uuid "445e63e5-652e-5dc8-8351-e2fbc1b14148" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b73478f8-b885-594b-a9a0-e27cc437e81a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465659} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8b414f-27f6-5450-99ad-7a22e6912793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465660} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e7ea1a-de3f-549d-b7d9-e591346c6e82" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77359e72-e6db-54da-84e0-5a07ac19909a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465661} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ea3dc-1b67-5809-a058-95b24fde0dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465661} :answer-field/id #uuid "993baea2-7ee4-5876-a225-396d9a3cd0af" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466674}] :question/id #uuid "71c46d34-a9b9-54b7-8de2-8c7deffeb5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-177667" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The number of rows in $A$ is not the same as the number of columns. So, it's not a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Note that\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not a square matrix, our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b180b5-cbd5-5b9a-ae2d-e655faa840d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484884} {:answer/id #uuid "2bad9be6-a82c-5f4f-879d-dcbfb4a2f3c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484905} {:answer/id #uuid "bae5ca7d-1994-5c77-8acf-ebf9f1ba4fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485218} {:answer/id #uuid "e09075e8-f3b4-55d6-af6b-f159bb382010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485291} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485340} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb63660-4233-5926-a45a-b277379f4cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485399}] :question/id #uuid "203918fb-bff3-5640-9116-ee4c833a081b" :question/math-academy-id "q-177668" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The number of rows in $A$ is not the same as the number of columns. So, it's not a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not a square matrix and ${A}^{T}\\cdot A\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fff5188-49f9-5ba0-bde2-420c0a8bf40b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484850} {:answer/id #uuid "5ceae71f-3b25-523c-b399-ef203fc61915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485024} {:answer/id #uuid "65bb6b5a-1475-52a9-b0fc-a90761104b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485039} {:answer/id #uuid "74086728-2a15-558c-9eda-23ae9a3e855c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485067} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485356} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f3276f-779b-51ad-9d6b-890a9e89a2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485469}] :question/id #uuid "46db878d-0e5d-50fb-979a-d499bbe2ee60" :question/math-academy-id "q-177659" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{24}{25} \\\\ \\frac{24}{25} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013b5339-64c6-5007-b26d-8e17a9af1e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484818} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5f1870-fd22-5be7-af97-1d34504dc1ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485087} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ab3e2b-fed0-5981-a65e-df0e8c2ddfca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485168} {:answer/id #uuid "e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485308} {:answer/id #uuid "eede04ef-d603-58e9-897e-2826d2f2ca05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485308} :answer-field/id #uuid "d87ebbb7-74a3-5ba5-93e4-063a3206f479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485459}] :question/id #uuid "83aaff63-f033-5323-bd52-af10976e5a16" :question/math-academy-id "q-177656" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484891} {:answer/id #uuid "658947d8-f94a-5959-8f98-7a5a5937a024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485038} {:answer/id #uuid "c5808f66-f6df-524e-9eaa-c92ca8711d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485241} {:answer/id #uuid "d001edcd-7aa6-5ff6-a64d-f2057575b857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485256} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb3e8ee-7783-5420-882a-066010a26592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484891} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f1d3ef9-793b-5e24-8e99-68db383cf524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485410}] :question/id #uuid "bb8ec734-9246-5393-99e6-34bea8046fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177661" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133504 :question/id #uuid "b87bd2f0-67da-5b9d-9e21-831afa44eec8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12948" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d97da6252422d33ef758793ec93d4ef85076fbaa524215ad19c709f42005aeff.svg)\n\nFind $|\\textrm{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(-2\\sqrt{3})\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}-2\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-18-2| \\\\  & =|-20| \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb197d48-db10-5005-a643-6196a02e7f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131505} {:answer/id #uuid "09fc5509-0fe6-5a43-83a3-eb571792902d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131507} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea43c74-a7de-5495-88c7-0382f008fbb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131508} {:answer/id #uuid "20045821-316a-5633-acd8-365f31e8c083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484876} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0f3828-98fe-56d1-a565-afe9f584dd2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131505} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fbdaad-a6a3-563a-99d3-49ed8677de91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131503}] :question/id #uuid "33946d4e-a787-5aee-914d-44804d2c4a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-39872" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}| \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b820cb-72ef-50ef-a9bf-f5e8a38636e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131510} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f6bb18-184a-5a98-bdf2-32973baa82c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131512} {:answer/id #uuid "26532a6d-633c-526a-a3c4-ae6120b78154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484887} {:answer/id #uuid "36d6ba13-23fd-551d-9a3a-a0cf24d03ce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484933} {:answer/id #uuid "53f9636f-f836-5a16-b4fe-9bd98143b7eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131512} :answer-field/id #uuid "219dc850-1ff5-58e7-b926-bbc34284f736" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131509}] :question/id #uuid "48e38c7e-484d-5cb3-85cb-dfcc3bab8451" :question/math-academy-id "q-39873" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-8\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a47111d-6c23-5b0a-91f9-9bb04923dabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25-\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351802} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce09dc-21df-5eb3-a895-49c7aebe4105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351952} {:answer/id #uuid "2f429717-4c5f-5e0a-a416-5943a1f7e75a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352002} {:answer/id #uuid "b67b2975-b129-51c2-a7fa-c3fb89bbbec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353132} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b042d5-c51b-5d9e-a235-9626ad575cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353132} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed11a05b-d987-571f-866e-9395d8d74355" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354223}] :question/id #uuid "ca01bd52-5594-59b2-b1c6-fbcc08e19094" :question/math-academy-id "q-84242" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|5\\cdot 5-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{2}| \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d68b51b-4591-54c7-ba81-5996ef57ea9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351828} {:answer/id #uuid "36c087e1-1ec5-5ffd-98e5-edae56ba3a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352075} {:answer/id #uuid "472676ce-88ce-5ad1-b7a6-1526b12b11aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352225} {:answer/id #uuid "a78b83e0-3032-57c6-b43b-90c469e33c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352989} {:answer/id #uuid "c932c08b-6582-59ca-ac0f-f2be376f9e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352225} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fb308b4-0bc8-54d6-a99a-efb8b9340eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354052}] :question/id #uuid "529b90b2-e399-56c8-81d1-f500bf1005f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-84253" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{37}} & \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{37}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{37}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{37}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & \\sqrt{6} \